+`dimos hardware can list` on macOS reports gs_usb adapters (`1d50:606f`,
+selected by USB serial) and PEAK-System PCAN-USB Pro FD (`0C72:0011`). The Pro
+FD is dual-channel; listing shows `PCAN_USBBUS1` and `PCAN_USBBUS2`. Those
+names are not OpenArm `--left-can-port` / `--right-can-port` values on macOS:
+`can-motor-control` only opens gs_usb there, and opening PEAK requires PEAK's
+MacCAN/PCBUSB `PCANBasic` library plus a PCAN bus backend that dimOS does not
+ship. On Linux, load `peak_usb` so the two channels appear as SocketCAN `can0`
+and `can1`, then `dimos hardware can setup can0` / `can1` and pass those
+interface names.
